// Pull request author: saakovv
// Change: new rule
// Title: Linux Ransomware File Artifact Indicators
// Sigma ID: d7f3e8b6-9a4c-4d08-e6f7-8b5a1c4d3e70
// Status: experimental | Level: critical
// Author: Ivan Saakov
// Date: 2026-05-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: impact, T1486
// Description: Detects creation or execution of files with extensions or names commonly associated with
//   ransomware payloads and ransom notes. This includes well-known ransomware families such as
//   Akira, LockBit, ALPHV, Babuk, and others. The detection focuses on interpreter-spawned processes
//   that access or create files with these indicators, which is a pattern seen in scripted
//   ransomware deployment during the impact phase of an attack.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely in production environments; security research or sandbox analysis
// References:
//   - https://www.cisa.gov/stopransomware
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e5bac28da3655c33390db7ef1503db8cd3babb5f/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_ransomware_artifacts.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains ".locked" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".crypt" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".akira" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".lockbit" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".alphv" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".babuk" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".helloKitty" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".royal_w" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".elsxir" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ROYALS") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "HOW_TO_DECRYPT" or ProcessCommandLine contains "README_FOR_RESTORE" or ProcessCommandLine contains "DECRYPT_INSTRUCTIONS" or ProcessCommandLine contains "RESTORE_FILES" or ProcessCommandLine contains "RANSOM_NOTE" or ProcessCommandLine contains "HOW_TO_BACK_FILES" or ProcessCommandLine contains "RECOVER_FILES_README" or ProcessCommandLine contains "HELP_DECRYPT")
